Given a plane $\alpha$ and a line $l$, consider the following statements:  
(1) If $l$ is perpendicular to two lines within $\alpha$, then $l \perp \alpha$;  
(2) If $l$ is perpendicular to all lines within $\alpha$, then $l \perp \alpha$;  
(3) If $l$ is perpendicular to two intersecting lines within $\alpha$, then $l \perp \alpha$;  
(4) If $l$ is perpendicular to countless lines within $\alpha$, then $l \perp \alpha$;  
(5) If $l$ is perpendicular to any line within $\alpha$, then $l \perp \alpha$. The correct number of statements is ( )
A: 2
B: 3
C: 4
D: 5

s:
(1) If $l$ is perpendicular to two parallel lines within $\alpha$, then it does not necessarily mean that $l \perp \alpha$, hence (1) is incorrect;  
(2) If $l$ is perpendicular to all lines within $\alpha$, according to the definition of line perpendicular to a plane, then $l \perp \alpha$, hence (2) is correct;  
(3) If $l$ is perpendicular to two intersecting lines within $\alpha$, according to the theorem for determining a line perpendicular to a plane, then $l \perp \alpha$, hence (3) is correct;  
(4) If $l$ is perpendicular to countless parallel lines within $\alpha$, then it does not necessarily mean that $l \perp \alpha$, hence (4) is incorrect;  
(5) If $l$ is perpendicular to any line within $\alpha$, according to the definition of line perpendicular to a plane, then $l \perp \alpha$, hence (5) is correct.  
Therefore, the correct choice is $\boxed{\text{B}}$.

